 # Volumetric Attribute and Density Formation
-
-
 ## Overview
-Volumetric Attribute and Density Formation is the family of methods that map conceptual or physical sources (meshes, point clouds, parametric functions, or raw data) into discrete or analytic volumetric representations suitable for rendering [G]. It solves the problem of converting continuous or sparse input data into a structured grid where each voxel stores specific attributes (density, velocity, size, or directional normals) required for Direct Volume Rendering (DVR) or simulation. It differs from its siblings by encompassing both the geometric occupancy determination (e.g., [Interior Voxelize](995-interior-voxelize.md)) and the assignment of physical or visual attributes (e.g., [Velocity Voxelization](3082-velocity-voxelization.md), [Anisotropic Voxelization](4331-anisotropic-voxelization.md)) to those voxels, rather than just binary occupancy.
